gpod-utils (1.5.4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Preserve chapter markers when copying m4b audiobooks

    gpod-cp now reads embedded chapter markers (title + start time) from
    the source file via ffmpeg and writes them into the iTunesDB's
    Itdb_Chapterdata for the track, so m4b audiobooks keep chapter
    navigation on the iPod. m4b was already accepted as an input (format
    support is codec-based, not extension-based, and libgpod preserves
    the source extension when copying to the iPod) but chapters were
    previously dropped entirely. Chapters are also restored after the
    transcode-rescan step for sources that need conversion (eg flac
    audiobooks), since the temp transcoded file won't carry them.

 -- Ilya Kargapolov <d3vil.st@gmail.com>  Sat, 04 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0200

